%% Connection lifecycle shared by USB (loopback) and Wi-Fi (LAN) transports.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant T as Tablet (InkBridgeClient)
  participant H as Mac (PeerConnection)

  T->>H: TCP connect (127.0.0.1:8765 via adb reverse, or mac-ip:8766)
  H->>T: auth.challenge {nonce (32 random bytes), required: false on USB / true on Wi-Fi}
  alt required
    T->>H: device.hello {…, auth = HMAC-SHA256(code, nonce)}
    alt HMAC valid
      H->>T: device.ready {host_name, session_id}
    else invalid / missing
      H->>T: error {code: auth_failed}
      H--xT: close · failure counted (5 in 60 s ⇒ LAN lockout)
      Note over T: ClientState.Failed — no retry loop
    end
  else not required
    T->>H: device.hello {…}
    H->>T: device.ready
  end

  par every 2 s, both directions
    H->>T: connection.ping {ping_id}
    T->>H: connection.pong {ping_id, echo_timestamp_ns}
  and
    T->>H: connection.ping
    H->>T: connection.pong
  end

  loop drawing
    T->>H: stroke.begin / stroke.point / stroke.end (ordered, sequenced)
  end

  Note over T,H: No inbound bytes for 7 s ⇒ either side closes.<br/>Client retries 250 → 500 → 1000 → 2000 ms (±20 % jitter),<br/>re-handshakes, then flushes events queued during the outage.
